run_eval: add the Antigravity (agy) eval adapter, correcting #27's claim

#27 shipped Codex/OpenCode eval adapters and claimed no Antigravity
adapter was possible, because Antigravity "does not reliably discover
project-local .agents/skills/ skills at all." That claim was wrong --
it conflated a real, separately-confirmed fact (a disable-model-
invocation-flagged skill is suppressed from Antigravity's self-reported
skill list, true for show-me, confirmed for #12) with a false one (an
unflagged skill at a project-local path isn't discovered at all, which
it is). Re-confirmed live, twice, while building deliver's own
cross-harness smoke tests (#24).

Adds _run_single_query_agy + _agy_event_indicates_trigger, same
architecture as the Codex/OpenCode adapters: a throwaway, uniquely-
named proxy skill under .agents/skills/, agy --output-format
stream-json --print for structured output, and a predicate recognizing
the step_update/tool_name=="view_file" event whose AbsolutePath points
at the proxy's SKILL.md -- confirmed live against real captured event
data. find_conflicting_installed_skill now also checks agy's real
global skill directory (~/.gemini/config/skills/) in addition to the
project-local path, since Antigravity reads both.

vendor/skill-creator/DISPOSITION.md records this as an explicit
correction, not a silent edit.

